  "mujoco_changes": "2026-10-12, on the soft contact class at a constant impedance: the one-hand hang instead of the fold (stages hang_release_table_pickup_stages, prefix hang {lift_m 0.32, pull_over}). With the released fold and tilt the ring stays hooked through both shoes' bends after the upper shoe is let go, and no release turn, other tilt or active pickup separated it (docs/rcb/families/horseshoe_ring.md). Now the right hand alone lifts the right shoe 0.32 m (its recorded grasp); the chain links and the left shoe hang from it, and the ring hangs on the hanging shoe. The left hand grasps the ring (first a grasp from which a direct way to a descent start exists), brings it level around the links above the shoe, lowers it along the hanging axis past the shoe's bend (the bore's long axis along the shoe's width: 2.3 mm to spare at best) and carries it into the goal. The right hand never lets go. The task, its separator and its success rule are unchanged. 2026-10-12, on the 32-facet cylinder prisms (64820cfbf): lifted straight up, the right shoe's open end carried the ring up with it (the ring, which at the birth lies flat around that end and both links, slid off it back to the table on the cylinders); the ring then hung around the held shoe's end, its top arc above it, and no way of the pull-over left it (every direct way pressed it 0.6-0.9 mm into the held shoe, the joint search ran out of budget). The early shed tilt (prefix hang shed_tilt_deg 30, shed_yaw_deg -90, shed_lift_m 0.12): at 0.12 m of lift the right hand turns the shoe -90 deg about the vertical through its grasp, pitches its eye end 30 deg down, holds 4 s, levels it, turns it back and lifts the rest; the ring slides off the end onto the links as before."
